  "id": "Wandsworth-2026_0115",
  "appeal_status": null,
  "appeal_start_date": "09/06/2026",
  "description": "Removal of an existing phone box and installation of street hub with illuminated digital advertisement screen to each side.",
  "development_type": "Other advertisements",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "Reason : 1 - The proposed Street Hub, by reason of its scale, design and location would fail to minimise street clutter, result in loss of public open space and harm to the character and appearance of the Conservation Area and the setting of heritage asset opposite. Furthermore, the hub would create an unnecessary obstruction of the public space, hindering the convenient and safe passage of pedestrians. Whilst the proposal would result in some facilities for the general public, these benefits are low and do not outweigh the harm identified. The proposal therefore fails to comply with the National Planning Policy Framework (2024), policies D3, D8, HC1, T2 and T4 of the London Plan (2021), policies LP1, LP3, LP9, LP22, LP49 and LP50 of the Local Plan (2023).\r\n",
    "Reason : 2 - In dealing with this application the Council has implemented the requirement in the National Planning Policy Framework to make available detailed advice in the form of our statutory policies in the Local Plan as well as offering a full pre application advice service. However, we have been unable to seek solutions to problems as the proposal is clearly contrary to our statutory policies and negotiation could not overcome the reasons for refusal."
  ],
